INT. LAUNDROMAT PAYPHONE ALCOVE - NIGHT

Buzzing light. One payphone. Quarters stacked on the shelf.

RAVINDRA "RAVI" SANDHU-OKORO (16, duffel on shoulder) grips the receiver. Beside him, his best friend KIKO TANAKA-MBEKI (16, sweatshirt, a bag of chips) leans on the wall.

MOTHER (V.O.)
(tinny, over the line)
Ravi? Where are you? It's past midnight.

RAVI
I'm fine, Mom. I'm with Kiko.

KIKO
^Hi, Mrs. Sandhu!

MOTHER (V.O.)
Is that Kiko? Put him on.

RAVI
He can't. He's, um. Eating.

MOTHER (V.O.)
Ravindra. Come home.

Ravi looks at his duffel. Looks at Kiko. Kiko shrugs and offers a chip.

RAVI
(quietly)
I'm coming, Mom. I'm just walking slow.

He hangs up. Takes a chip. They stand in the buzzing light.
